{"message": "Successfully loaded the following tools: [StructuredTool(name='you-search', description='Search the web for current information, facts, news, and sources.\n>\nBest for: current events, facts about people, companies, and organizations, finding primary sources, verifying claims.\nReturns: ranked results with URLs and snippets — read them with you-contents before answering; snippets are not page content.\n>\nQuery tips:\n- One intent per search, phrased naturally: "tariff exemptions for semiconductor imports 2026" — not a question, not a pile of synonyms.\n- Inline filters are mapped automatically: `site:cdc.gov`, `lang:fr`, `loc:DE`.\n- On zero results, don\'t repeat the query: drop exact-phrase ("quoted") constraints first, then widen — keep domain filters unless the domain itself was wrong. Or read the best prior result with you-contents.', args_schema={'type': 'object', '$schema': 'https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema', 'properties': {'query': {'type': 'string', 'minLength': 1, 'description': 'Short natural-language phrase describing one thing to find, e.g. "tariff exemptions for semiconductor imports 2026". Inline `site:`, `lang:`, `loc:` filters are mapped automatically. Max 50 words / 400 characters after operator mapping.'}, 'count': {'default': 30, 'description': 'Max results per section', 'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 1, 'maximum': 100}, 'freshness': {'description': 'Limit results to a recent window. Use it when recency matters — news, prices, releases, "this year" — and omit it for evergreen facts. Pass a named bucket (`day`, `week`, `month`, `year`) or a date range `YYYY-MM-DDtoYYYY-MM-DD`. If the query already names a timeframe, the broader of the two wins, so this can only widen, never narrow, the query phrase.', 'type': 'string'}, 'offset': {'description': 'Pagination offset, in multiples of count. count=5 and offset=1 returns results 5–10. Range 0–9. Omit on the first page.', 'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 0, 'maximum': 9}, 'extraction': {'default': 'highlights', 'description': 'Extraction mode. "highlights" (default) returns query-relevant passages; "none" returns plain snippets; "full_page" crawls each result and returns full page content.', 'type': 'string', 'enum': ['none', 'highlights', 'full_page']}, 'knowledge': {'description': 'Include licensed knowledge results relevant to the query. core requests factual answers alongside web and news results; matching results appear in results.knowledge.', 'type': 'string', 'enum': ['core']}, 'safesearch': {'description': 'Content-moderation filter. Omit to let the API default (moderate) apply.', 'type': 'string', 'enum': ['off', 'moderate', 'strict']}, 'extraction_source': {'description': "Where full-page content comes from when extraction is 'full_page'. 'cache' is included in base cost, 'fetch' bills at livecrawl rates, 'blend' bills only for pages not in cache.", 'type': 'string', 'enum': ['cache', 'fetch', 'blend']}, 'crawl_timeout': {'description': 'Max seconds to wait for page content when extraction is full_page (1–60). Omit for the default 10.', 'type': 'integer', 'minimum': 1, 'maximum': 60}, 'exclude_domains': {'description': 'Domains to exclude from search results (up to 500). Cannot be combined with inline `site:` filters, which map to include_domains.', 'maxItems': 500, 'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}}, 'required': ['query']}, tags=['langchain_tool'], metadata={'title': None, 'readOnlyHint': True, 'destructiveHint': False, 'idempotentHint': None, 'openWorldHint': True, '_meta': {'co.baseten/llm-controllable-params-default': ['query', 'freshness'], 'com.you.com/search': {'description': 'Host-supplied search overrides. Send an object under the `com.you.com/search` key in tools/call params._meta (or X-Search-* HTTP headers); every field is optional and wins over model-supplied arguments. Host-only fields (language, country, include_domains, boost_domains) are settable here and never by the model.', 'schema': {'$schema': 'http